  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c9f2e8e5b57bd4bd99f33dd56077c2d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: KB_007_StaleTerminalIp
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: POSTechSupport::POSTechSupport.Data.KnowledgeArticleSO
  articleId: KB-007
  title: Register is healthy but POS still refuses it
  category: 1
  content: "POS keeps a registered roster of terminal addresses. After a router reboot
    the terminal can pick up a new DHCP address while POS still has the old one on
    file \u2014 the terminal is on the right network with a valid IP, and POS rejects
    it anyway. The fault is on the POS side, not the terminal side.\nCompare POS
    Terminal \u25B8 Status (the terminal's actual IP) against POS Manager \u25B8
    Connections (what POS has registered), then re-register the current address.
    The real IP is shown for you \u2014 never guess it. Keep this separate from a
    staff member who cannot log in: that is a role/assignment problem on one account,
    not a connectivity problem."
  relatedErrorCodes: []
  guidanceForIssueIds:
  - P7
